Verification date: 2026-08-12 (Europe/Moscow)

Environment
-----------
Python 3.12.13
MuJoCo 3.11.0
MediaPipe 0.10.35
OpenCV 5.0.0
websocket-client 1.9.0

Automated checks
----------------
python -m compileall -q src tests tools: PASS
python -m pytest -q: 150 passed in 95.82s
git diff --check: PASS

Grounded physics and motor-control checks
-----------------------------------------
Both foot collision geoms contact the ground in fixed and free scenes.
Grounded-fixed normal force after settling: about 28.8 N.
Robot source mass: 2.933134 kg; expected weight at 9.81 m/s^2: 28.77 N.
Visual soles and collision soles remain within about 1 mm of the ground.
No non-ground proxy self-contact is present in the home pose.

The free-base controller writes only the canonical 20 motor position targets.
It never writes the floating-base qpos, creates a weld, or applies external force.
Support transitions are gated by measured sole loads, touchdown, base tilt and
base angular speed. Opposite-leg requests use a bounded one-slot queue and are
executed only after returning through DOUBLE_SUPPORT.

Coordinate/retargeting checks
-----------------------------
MediaPipe camera axes are treated as +X image-right, +Y image-down, +Z away.
Robot physical front is MuJoCo -X; robot left is +Y; robot up is +Z.
Semantic FK tests verify that a human right-arm/right-leg forward motion moves
only the matching robot limb toward physical robot front, rather than merely
checking a motor-array sign. Angular deltas use shortest-path wrapping at +/-pi.
The Unity FRONT camera/front_motor and converted long-toe geometry independently
confirm the -X robot-front convention. Tasks hidden during explicit neutral
calibration remain unavailable until recalibration; a moving pose cannot become
a lazy per-task zero.

Visual checks
-------------
21 Unity FBX links converted to 21 visual-only Wavefront OBJ meshes.
Meshes: 259,480 render vertices; 122,251 triangles.
Both MJCF scenes compile with separate render groups:
  group 0 = environment
  group 1 = visual OBJ meshes
  group 2 = physical collision proxies
Offscreen visual and joints views rendered successfully. A synchronized
human/MediaPipe versus actual grounded-fixed MuJoCo contact sheet was generated
as artifacts/ik-pose-comparison.png. Raw IK fidelity over the bundled clip and
four external public-domain clips is stored in artifacts/pose-fidelity.json.

